    "body": "Orchestrator note for the fix round (recommended option taken under the Autonomous Work Law, the maintainer may overrule): a machine-DEFAULT holder is an assumption, not something the user mounted, so it must never judge looser than the stand-in cylinder a bare tool gets today - floor the default holder's bands at the old cylinder (or judge the union). A holder the user picks explicitly is the real one and wins. Correct the decision record and the 'never looser' test comment, and pin the band just above the shank (wall 20 mm off axis, 55-65 mm above the tip) on a BT30 and a TTS machine. The `camcraft-post -> camcraft-tools` dependency stays a maintainer question.",
