    "body": "Review-fix round pushed (head 7594010a; origin/main 3bd54fc9 merged in, no rebase). Still a draft.\n\n- **Blocker fixed.** A machine-DEFAULT holder is judged by the union of its drawn bands and the tool's stand-in `holder_d` x `holder_len` cylinder (`HolderProfile::floored`, in `tool_body::judged`); an explicitly picked holder keeps its real shape. Which one is stored as `ToolBody::machine_default` (set only by `AddTool`'s default door, in the add's undo step; additive `\"machine_default\": true` on the tool body in the project file - absent = explicit, so older files' holders count as picked; also a term in the op stamp).\n- **Pinned** on BT30 and TTS in the review's band (wall 20 mm off axis, 55-65 mm above the tip): `crates/tools` `an_assumed_holder_convicts_the_band_above_the_shank_where_the_bare_tool_does`; app `an_assumed_default_never_judges_looser_than_the_bare_tool` (bare > 0 hits, default >= bare, explicit pick 0) and `an_assumed_holder_stays_assumed_through_the_file`.\n- **Wording corrected**: decision record (\"stricter\" removed, maintainer's rule recorded) and the reach test's comment.\n- **Dependency removed** (maintainer reversal): `camcraft-post` no longer depends on `camcraft-tools`; the post reader takes a `HolderLookup` (`&dyn Fn(&str) -> Result<HolderInfo, String>`, `HolderInfo { name, taper }`) from its caller; the app passes `machine::holder_lookup` through its own `parse_mch` / `tooling_refusals` / `tooling_refusal`. Refusal texts unchanged; `Cargo.lock` back to main's.\n- **Review note 1**: a stored default holder that no longer resolves is refused naming `tooling.default_holder` (`a_stored_default_that_no_longer_resolves_is_refused_by_key`).\n\nTargeted suites and clippy green (list in the PR body); batch tier not re-run.\n",
